  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "World creators should be able to set avatar limits for public instances of their world, e.g. set 200k polygons as the maximum for one avatar to avoid their world getting raided by crasher avatars all the time or simply to control the overal performance of their world. Private instances should be unaffected by this. The same should be possible for dynamic bone count etc. - this would also motivate users to use more optimized avatars and increase the experience for everyone.",
